// expect: refuse E_PatternInexhaustive
// A LITERAL IN PARAMETER POSITION IS SILENTLY A WILDCARD. `(0) => 1` is an
// arm that takes only 0 (SYNTAX §«Function literals»: a pattern in
// parameter position is an arm on the argument), so it is inexhaustive and
// must refuse. Today the lambda's parameters are parsed as expressions and
// reinterpreted, a literal becomes `_`, and `f(5)` answers 1 (measured
// 2026-09-25, clean check).
//
// Retires when parameters parse as patterns from the start, which is the
// same change that gives every parameter a binder node
// (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
fn main() = {
  let f = (0) => 1
  f(5)
}
